{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02279",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 5.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Good evening, um, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.57,
      "end_seconds": 12.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.04,
      "end_seconds": 23.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Mainly a severe painful red eye. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.56,
      "end_seconds": 28.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.61,
      "end_seconds": 36.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "About a week, I think... sorry, about two weeks, I got that wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.99,
      "end_seconds": 46.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.97,
      "end_seconds": 73.1,
      "duration_seconds": 24.13,
      "text": "It, It happens on and off. Dim light definitely sets it off. It feels mild to me. Oh, you know, and blurred vision with halos. Had that since yesterday. Oh, as for blurred vision with halos, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.98,
      "end_seconds": 80.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any injury, contact lens or discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.76,
      "end_seconds": 88.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "I mean, no injury, contact lens or discharge, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.89,
      "end_seconds": 91.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.24,
      "end_seconds": 98.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.49,
      "end_seconds": 110.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.76,
      "end_seconds": 113.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.52,
      "end_seconds": 119.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.97,
      "end_seconds": 124.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "So, yes, trimethoprim, it it gives me itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.45,
      "end_seconds": 137.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.23,
      "end_seconds": 151.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.4,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I work in accounts at a hospital. I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.89,
      "end_seconds": 156.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.43,
      "end_seconds": 162.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I've had heart disease for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.23,
      "end_seconds": 171.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart disease in your file as well. What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.21,
      "end_seconds": 177.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "I take aspirin, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.14,
      "end_seconds": 181.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.05,
      "end_seconds": 183.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "It's 75 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.69,
      "end_seconds": 188.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.28,
      "end_seconds": 190.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.91,
      "end_seconds": 195.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.39,
      "end_seconds": 215.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "The right eye is red, the pupil is fixed and mid-sized, and the eye feels rock hard."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.68,
      "end_seconds": 224.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.9,
      "end_seconds": 251.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at acute angle-closure glaucoma or a severe infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.85,
      "end_seconds": 294.52,
      "duration_seconds": 32.67,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an urgent eye pressure check because of acute glaucoma. You'll be taking acetazolamide, 500 milligrams, now, single dose. That's for acute glaucoma. This is a sight-threatening emergency, I am sending you to the eye casualty now. I'd like you to see the eye emergency service as well, and I'll write the referral. Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.26,
      "end_seconds": 297.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.71,
      "end_seconds": 303.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Please come and and see me straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.41,
      "end_seconds": 308.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.01,
      "end_seconds": 316.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.75,
      "end_seconds": 325.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "So, I take the acetazolamide, 500 milligrams, now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.39,
      "end_seconds": 332.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "so, yes, exactly right. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.49,
      "end_seconds": 336.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "well, no, that's all. Thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.55,
      "end_seconds": 339.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}